\label{conv:package}
A \emph{theory package} is a tuple $(Z,\,f,\,E,\,\mathcal A)$ consisting of a carrier $Z$;
a \emph{lens} $f\colon Z\to X$ recording what an observer sees of a carrier object (its
\emph{definability content} is the family of predicates constant on the fibers of $f$);
a \emph{completion} (or \emph{packaging}) endomap $E\colon Z\to Z$, typically idempotent,
whose fixed points are the \emph{objects} the package recognizes; and an \emph{audit}
$\mathcal A$, a monotone certificate.

