expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{thm:tfae}
For a finite directed graph $G=(V,\to)$ the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}\itemsep0pt
  \item $G$ is acyclic (no directed cycle, including no self-loop);
  \item there is an audit $\rho\colon V\to\mathbb N$ strictly decreasing along edges:
  $u\to w\Rightarrow\rho(w)<\rho(u)$;
  \item every nonempty $S\subseteq V$ has a $\to$-minimal element.
\end{enumerate}

