expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{thm:nonattain}
Let $G$ be any finitely generated completion rule and $A_0\subseteq\mathrm{HF}$ any seed. Then:
\begin{enumerate}\itemsep0pt
  \item no finite iterate $A_n=G^n(A_0)$ contains an inductive set as an element;
  \item if $G$ is additionally idempotent (a closure operator on families), the iteration
  stabilizes after one step, $G^n(A_0)=G(A_0)$ for $n\ge 1$;
  \item the $\omega$-limit family $A_\omega=\bigcup_n A_n$ satisfies $A_\omega\subseteq\mathrm{HF}$, and
  $\omega\notin A_\omega$; admitting $\omega$ as a completed object requires a rule step outside
  the finitely generated class.
\end{enumerate}

