\begin{description}[leftmargin=!,labelwidth=0.28\textwidth,itemsep=3pt]
\item[No finite derivation of $\mathsf{ZF}$ or $\mathsf{ZFC}$.] The finite tier reaches $\mathrm{HF}$;
the infinitary axioms enter only as named purchases.
\item[No consistency proof.] Classical consistency and relative-consistency content remains in
the cited literature.
\item[No new independence theorem.] The forcing section reorganizes Cohen forcing through the
paper's lens language; it does not extend the classical theorem set.
\item[No uniqueness of $\mathsf{ZFC}$.] The CH instance and countermodel atlas explicitly leave
room for alternative completions and instruments.
\item[No metaphysical universe claim.] The paper treats sets as packages under a membership lens;
it does not assert an antecedent ontology of sets.
\item[No unification theorem.] The G\"odel--Cohen saturation/extension comparison is
discussion-grade framing, supported by theorem-backed halves but not itself a new metatheorem.
\end{description}

